    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1683">

                <pb facs="1330" n="1320" sameAs="frus:frus1949v08/pg1320"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1115/8–1849: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in the United
                        Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Douglas</hi>)<anchor n="47"
                        xml:id="d1683-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-08-18T19:00:00-04:00">August 18, 1949—7
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2961. Upon closing any US Govt Dipl or Con estab in China where Brit have Dipl or
                    Con reps Dept would also desire ref Deptel 2925 16th Brit Consulates afford
                    Amcitizens protection similar that afforded Brit natls. Conceivable Amcitizens
                    rendered destitute might also require financial or other assistance but criteria
                    for eligibility receive financial assistance and limitations upon maxima amounts
                    would be details for future solution based upon Brit Consuls’ recommendations
                    through FonOff to Dept for its consideration.</p>
                <p>Emb requested formally inquire FonOff whether Brit willing undertake this service
                    for AmGovt and if so will inform its Consuls China in foregoing sense. Matter
                    considered urgent. Keep Dept informed.<anchor n="48" xml:id="d1683-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1683-f1" n="47" type="source" xml:id="d1683-f1-content">
                <p>Repeated to the Embassy in China, the Chargé in China, the Vice Consul at
                    Chungking, the Consul General at Hankow, the Vice Consul at Kunming, the Consul
                    General at Peiping, the Consul at Shanghai, the Consul General at Tientsin, the
                    Vice Consul at Tihwa, and the Consul at Tsingtao as telegrams Nos. 985, telCan
                    597, 72, 62, 70, 557, 1646, 251, 123, and 243, respectively.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1683-f2" n="48" xml:id="d1683-f2-content">
                <p>Correspondence with the British Foreign Office by which the arrangement was
                    concluded was transmitted to the Department by the Ambassador in the United
                    Kingdom in his despatch No. 1390, August 24; received August 29, not
                    printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
